notes:
MOD-021 builds Layercake.silv_daily_count_adjustment, the two as-known-at table functions and the review view. All 23 tests pass: the 17 in test_MOD021 and 6 in test_MOD021_dev. They failed before the build because the objects did not exist.

Table: adjustment_id is a clustered identity primary key. The unique constraint is UQ on (run_id, [date], region, country_id, gender_id, grade, membership_status_id). CK_..._any_change rejects a row whose seven changes are all 0. IX_silv_daily_count_adjustment_date_written_at on ([date], written_at), with the cell and change columns included, serves the functions.

fn_silv_daily_count_detail_as_known_at is an inline table function. It stacks the stored detail rows on top of the negated adjustments written strictly after @as_known_at, within the date range, and groups by cell. A stored row is always returned, including one of all zeros. A cell found only in the history is returned when any of its seven figures is not 0 at T. A NULL parameter, or @date_from after @date_to, returns no rows.

fn_silv_daily_count_as_known_at sums the detail function by [date], region and grade.

The review view uses CROSS APPLY VALUES to give one row per non-zero measure. measure_name is varchar(30) NOT NULL; the ISNULL is there only to make the column NOT NULL.

Unit tests cover:
- several changes to one cell around T, and a stored row of zeros;
- a removed cell whose only figure at T is a lapse, and one removed before T;
- a reversed date range;
- the daily function, where Practising -1 / Retired +1 cancel out, region and grade stay separate, and a history-only cell gets its own row;
- the review view's column types.

No load writes the table yet; MOD-022 adds that. The down script drops the view and both functions. It drops the table when it is empty and renames it to _rolledback_MIG0023 when it holds rows.

Test-first: the first run had 0 of 17 of the Tester's tests passing; the final run passed 17 of 17 and 6 unit test(s), in 4 run(s).
